  "plain": "The mathematician Eric Weinstein argues that in the 1940s gifted wartime science administrators such as Vannevar Bush built structures for running American research, and that these worked well but the knowledge of what they were was never passed on, so they carry on like a zombie. Weinstein offers this as his own reading, without naming a source. If he is right, parts of US science could still be run by systems that no one in charge fully understands."
